Z||000001||GT Bastard||04-08-2001||10:55 AM||||I've seen a couple on the roads here.  I can't wait to race one when I get my SE rebuilt!||||reg||1
Z||000002||KRMFiero||04-08-2001||11:10 AM||||They look nice, they are fast (electronicly goverened to 130mph, but you can disable the govener and it does 165mph flat out).   i have not seen a WRX on the road yet, just dealer ship. I know someone that has a regular Impreza RS and that is one quick car heh I wouldnt want to attemp to race it with my fiero||||reg||1
Z||000003||stimpy||04-08-2001||11:52 AM||||I think they are actually puck-ugly, but 237hp, all-wheel drive... Yes, I want one!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Black88GT||04-08-2001||02:55 PM||||I can't understand why they don't offer a 2 door?  Personally I would rather have an Integra GSR or Type R for the price of those ugly 4 door WRX's.  Yes the WRX is an awesome car but its just not good looking and pretty expensive.  I like how all the guys in Car and Driver said "I have to get me one of these" hehe, must be fun to drive!<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD - MAFOA<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://88database.homestead.com/files/AF.gif">  <BR><I>"Once you go black, you never go back..."</I>||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FST2M6||04-09-2001||08:28 AM||||my friend just traded in his S2000 for a WRX. Pics and track time slips will come soon! his S had nitrous and 19s"... the WRX had 280miiles on it whae i saw him friday and it's already got an EVC IV (boost controller, Apexi N1 exhaust HKS intake and turbo timer! he sure didn't waste any time voiding the warranty on that one!... <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/s2000.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/s2000.jpg</A> <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 04-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Phantom Rage||04-10-2001||04:09 AM||||My friend has the WRX wagon.  Man that thing is deceptively fast.  It doesn't feel like you are really moving that fast, but from a visual perspective you can see it wheel in other cars fast! <BR>The WRX also has some serious grip; so far he has been unable to break the wheels loose, except for in the sand. As for the turns, he takes them pretty quick with out much tire fuss, if any.  The ride is firm yet overall smooth.  <BR>As for creature comforts, it’s quite comfy with room for five adults; the center rear passenger even gets a shoulder restraint seat belt.  It even comes with some extra goodies such as a Momo shift knob, steering wheel, and some cool looking drilled pedals.<BR>The only gripe as of far is the tranny, which seems to be its Achilles heel.  The shifter is a little notchy and clutch engagement could be a bit softer, but that’s probably due to a high performance clutch or something like that.    <P>Overall, I think it is on hell of a bang for the buck automobile.  I just hope that we get to see the STi here in the states sometime soon.  <BR>||||reg||7
